WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.099
Devil's advocacy involves deliberately questioning assumptions and conclusions to identify weaknesses in reasoning.

00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:08.945
Red team thinking introduces alternative perspectives that challenge prevailing narratives.

00:00:08.945 --> 00:00:12.790
These approaches should not create conflict for its own sake.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.635
Their purpose is improving analytical quality before decisions are made.

00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:21.250
Constructive challenge works best when it is focused on the reasoning, evidence,

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.557
and assumptions rather than personal disagreement.

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:27.018
The goal is sharper analysis, not winning an argument.

00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:32.017
Used well, devil's advocacy and red team thinking help teams notice blind spots,

00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:33.940
test confidence, and strengthen recommendations.
